femto patch for swash 0.2.6
Subject: scale: hint for grayscale instead of horizontal LCD subpixels

The scaler's Skrifa hinting mode is a private constant:
HintingMode::Smooth { lcd_subpixel: Some(LcdLayout::Horizontal), .. }.
The public scaler API has a hinting on/off switch but no way to choose the
mode.

Set lcd_subpixel: None (and drop the now unused LcdLayout import). Smooth
hinting and preserve_linear_metrics are unchanged.

femto renders to an e-paper panel with one coverage value per pixel and no
RGB subpixels, so LCD-targeted hinting is the wrong mode for it.

--- a/src/scale/hinting_cache.rs
+++ b/src/scale/hinting_cache.rs
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 use skrifa::{
     instance::{NormalizedCoord, Size},
     outline::{
-        HintingInstance, HintingMode, LcdLayout, OutlineGlyphCollection, OutlineGlyphFormat,
+        HintingInstance, HintingMode, OutlineGlyphCollection, OutlineGlyphFormat,
     },
 };
 
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 }
 
 const HINTING_MODE: HintingMode = HintingMode::Smooth {
-    lcd_subpixel: Some(LcdLayout::Horizontal),
+    lcd_subpixel: None,
     preserve_linear_metrics: true,
 };
 
